%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sherry_Victim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Sherry
  isScammer: 0
  steps:
  - npcLine: "I\u2019m helping my great-grandfather secure his digital life, and
      it made me realize my own security is a mess. I use the same password for everything!
      What should I do first?"
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Security is about building layers. What''s the
      foundation of a good defense?'
    choices:
    - text: Use a password manager to generate and store unique, strong passwords
        for every account.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Change all your passwords to your birthday so you never forget them.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -20
    - text: Just use your email password for every other site to keep it simple.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: "Okay, I\u2019ve got a password manager. Now, how do I stop my phone
      from being flooded with these 'Scam Likely' calls?"
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Preventing the initial contact is key. How do
      scammers even get your number?'
    choices:
    - text: Search for yourself on data broker sites and follow their opt-out processes.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Register for the National Do Not Call Registry; that will stop all scam
        calls forever.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
    - text: Answer every call and yell at the scammers until they take you off their
        list.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
  - npcLine: What about social media? I love sharing my Aikido progress and photos
      of my Unity game development. Is that a risk?
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Visibility is a double-edged sword. You can share,
      but you should control *who* sees it.'
    choices:
    - text: Set your profiles to 'Private' and only allow people you know to follow
        you.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Delete your social media accounts entirely; there's no safe way to use
        them.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Keep them public so you can build a bigger following for your game.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: I heard something about 'Two-Factor Authentication.' Is that really
      worth the extra effort of typing in a code every time?
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: It''s the single most effective way to stop someone
      who already has your password.'
    choices:
    - text: Yes, enable 2FA on all important accounts, especially your email and
        banking.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: No, it's just a way for companies to track your phone number.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Only use it for your university portal; other sites don't really matter.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: "If I get a call from my 'bank' and it looks like their real number,
      but I\u2019m not sure, what\u2019s my best move?"
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Your habits on the phone are just as important
      as your technical settings.'
    choices:
    - text: Hang up and call the bank back using the official number on the back
        of your card.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Stay on the line and ask them to verify their identity by giving you
        your SSN.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Ask them to text you a link to a 'secure chat' instead.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "I feel like I\u2019m becoming paranoid. Is it enough to just have a
      good antivirus program?"
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Antivirus is great for malware, but it doesn''t
      stop social engineering or data leaks.'
    choices:
    - text: Antivirus is just one layer; habits like 2FA and privacy settings are
        more effective against vishing.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Yes, a good antivirus will block all scam calls and identity theft attempts.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Antivirus is actually a scam itself; you should never use it.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: -5
  - npcLine: I found myself on a data broker site listing my age, address, and my
      'boyfriend's' name. How do I keep this from coming back?
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: Persistence is the name of the game with data
      brokers.'
    choices:
    - text: Check these sites every few months and re-request removal if you reappear.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Sue the data broker in small claims court so they stop listing you.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Ignore it; once you've opted out once, the law says they can't come back.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: My great-grandfather is asking if he should use a VPN. Does that help
      with vishing?
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: VPNs are for network privacy, but they don''t
      hide your phone number from scammers.'
    choices:
    - text: It helps with browsing privacy, but it won't stop scammers from calling
        or texting you.
      type: good
      pointValue: 10
    - text: Yes, a VPN will encrypt your phone calls and make you invisible to scammers.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: It's only useful if you're traveling out of the country.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: "I think I\u2019ve got a solid combination of habits now. Password manager,
      2FA, private social media, and data broker check-ups."
    assistantLine: 'Internal Voice: That is a ''defense-in-depth'' strategy. You
      are now a much harder target.'
    choices:
    - text: This combination effectively reduces my likelihood of being successfully
        targeted.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: I'm 100% immune to all scams now that I've done this.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'll go back to my Unity game. My dialogue script isn't going to write
        itself!
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  successEnding: "Correct! You identified that a combination of habits\u2014setting
    profiles to private, using unique passwords, enabling 2FA, and opting out of
    data brokers\u2014is the most effective way to reduce your risk."
  failureEnding: Incorrect. You relied too heavily on single solutions like antivirus
    or the Do Not Call registry, which do not protect against the diverse tactics
    used in vishing and social engineering.
